{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFZ5nPkfk79h2aRPmcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The recovery middleware now handles a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` the same way it handles a broken connection. It logs one short line with no stack trace and aborts the request without writing a 500 or calling the user's recovery handler. That matches how `net/http` treats this sentinel value. It also catches wrapped forms of the error, because it checks with `errors.Is`.\n\n- **Change:** `recovery.go:71` marks this panic as a broken connection.\n- **Test:** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. It checks that the status the handler set (204) is kept and that the log has no \"panic recovered\" stack dump.\n- **Result:** the `TestPanic*` tests fail without the fix and pass with it (gate passed).\n\nI only ran those `TestPanic*` tests, not the full suite. One behaviour change to know about: custom recovery handlers are no longer called for `ErrAbortHandler` panics."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":33412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1234,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d3b692a-dcf4-4b87-bd96-d077322c6061","uuid":"dffb06ef-928c-4026-916e-762aea04ed3e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:26:09.989Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFZ5YkhYoXcHyXQmmQN"}
